{
  "_about": "Build 2026-11-21a (test 57's fixes, the tester's wishes and art build B in one build, the user's pick, on top of 2026-11-17a: the bike drawn again in third person after your body; the free look on the right mouse button and in third person, the game's aim blocked while riding; the field kit's bike held on every model the menu has, turned only to a slot the highlight rests on, the wheel zooming anywhere and a drag off the lists turning it; the hand's copy of a holstered weapon hidden, the seat pose kept through a third-person put-away and a first-person draw, the handgun note judged on the weapon held; the coast twice as long and gradual, the gears in even steps; the Wear slot's seven looks on two new shells, three muddy tyres, a badge patch on the front fender, the headlamp in five colours (the lens and the beam), the Nuka-Cola and Red Rocket badges, the 3D Enclave helmet on the Enclave's flag and the 3D Brotherhood helmet between two cogs, the colour plates' top line centred), packaged on 2026-11-10a's package as the asset base with nine overlays laid over it in this order (OVERLAY=<1>:<2>:...:<9>, the later winning): 2026-11-17a's six, unchanged (/opt/cmb/assets15b/Data, /opt/cmb/assets16a/a/Data, /opt/cmb/assets16a/b/Data, /opt/cmb/assets16a/c/Data, /opt/cmb/assets17a/badges/Data, /opt/cmb/assets17a/plates/Data), then the shells unit's (/opt/cmb/assets21a/shells/Data: the five nifs by look_shells.py, static_wear, fork_wear and fork_badgeFront appended and the rear fender's patch raised, and the three shapes' six own invisible materials; it replaces 16a's a files of those names), the wear unit's (/opt/cmb/assets21a/wear/Data: the seven looks' 42 textures and 28 materials and the three muddy tyres' 6 diffuses and 12 materials by look_wear.py, all new) and the art2d unit's (/opt/cmb/assets21a/art2d/Data: badges_d/_n/_s.dds by bike_art.py --badges and look_badges.py and plates_d/_s.dds by bike_art.py --plates and look_plates.py, replacing 17a's badges and plates files of those names; badge_nukacola.bgsm and badge_redrocket.bgsm; the headlamp's eight lens materials and three lens textures by look_lamp.py). No two of the new overlays' files overlap, and each overlay's SHA256SUMS matches its files. Keys starting with _ are comments. What differs from the 2026-11-17a package, in two kinds: (1) the commit's own shipped files, checked against the commit by the tracked-files check and never listed in vs_previous (verify_zips.py --list-changes compares only the assets and the compiled scripts): Data/CommonwealthMotorbike.esp, Data/MCM/Config/CommonwealthMotorbike/config.json, Data/F4SE/Plugins/CMB_Slope.ini, Data/Scripts/Source/User/CMB_ControllerScript.psc, CMB_GearRestoreF4SE.psc and CMB_LookF4SE.psc, and Data/F4SE/Plugins/CMB_Slope.dll once the build's DLL is committed (the package takes the DLL from the commit, so tools/f4se-slope/build.sh's DLL has to be committed first; git diff --stat 24b2368 <the build's commit> -- Data lists them); keybinds.json is 2026-11-17a's; (2) the compiled scripts and assets, below (vs_previous): ten files changed, 107 added and three compiled scripts.",

