  "_vs_previous": "What verify_zips.py --list-changes compares: the assets (the files under Data/Meshes/CMB, Textures/CMB, Materials/CMB, Sound/FX/CMB and the riding clips' folder) and the compiled scripts (Data/Scripts/*.pex, by their code, not their headers) against the 2026-11-17a package. Ten files differ, each with its sha256 in this package (the overlays' SHA256SUMS, the units' notes list the same): the five nifs (look_shells.py; 2026-11-17a's CMB_BikeParked 4ebca10637..., CMB_BikeView 4714277161..., CMB_BikeWorn edc7b915d7..., CMB_BikeWornRider ea52130b06..., CMB_BikeWornRiderF a72fccaa1c...), the badge atlas (badges_d/_n/_s.dds, the same sizes: Nuka-Cola and Red Rocket in the spare cells [0,4] and [1,4], the Enclave flag and the Brotherhood cogs grounds; 2026-11-17a's 5c73f6ae14..., 6e5a213664..., 57d95c3fca...) and plates_d/_s.dds (the four colour plates' top line centred, the same sizes; 2026-11-17a's 431397940f..., f5e6afb502...; plates_n.dds and plate_p.dds are 2026-11-17a's). 107 files are new, each with its sha256 as its unit's tool wrote it (two runs give the same). Every sound and clip is 2026-11-17a's, and so are the other textures and materials. Three compiled scripts differ, their sources having changed: CMB_ControllerScript (the Wear, Front fender badge and Headlamp slots, the headlamp's beam per colour, GunNoteSure's note), CMB_LookF4SE (the three slots' globals) and CMB_GearRestoreF4SE (WornGun), null accepting their bytes (their headers carry the packaged commit's time); the other nine keep their code under a new header. The commit's own files that change (CMB_Slope.dll and CMB_Slope.ini, the ESP, the MCM's config.json, the three .psc: _about) are not in this block.",
